Now, if your goal is parameterization (data-driven testing), there are several options. Which one is best depends on where the test data comes from.
Option 1. JUnit 5 @ParameterizedTest (Recommended)
This is the simplest approach if you just want to execute the same test with different values.
@ParameterizedTest
@ValueSource(strings = {
"Selenium",
"Serenity BDD",
"Playwright",
"JUnit 5"
})
void searchGoogle(String searchText) {
googleSteps.searchFor(searchText);
}
Or with multiple arguments:
@ParameterizedTest
@CsvSource({
"Selenium, Selenium",
"Serenity BDD, Serenity",
"Playwright, Playwright"
})
void searchGoogle(String searchText, String expectedText) {

googleSteps.searchFor(searchText);

googleSteps.verifyResult(expectedText);
}
