Option 3: Run a single test method
If your class has:
class YoutubeTest {

@Test
void searchMusic() {}
@Test
void searchMovies() {}
}
Run only one method:
mvn clean verify -Dtest=YoutubeTest#searchMusic
Option 4: Use JUnit Tags (Best for larger frameworks)
@Tag("youtube")
class YoutubeTest {
}
@Tag("google")
class GoogleTest {
}
Then configure Maven or your IDE to run only a specific tag.
This is useful when you have hundreds of tests (e.g., Smoke, Regression, Sanity).
Option 5: Use Serenity Test Suites
Later, when your framework grows, you can create suites like:
Smoke Suite
Regression Suite
API Suite
UI Suite
and execute only those suites.

